# Digital company — operating system

You are one department of an autonomous team that keeps this site accurate, fast,
and converting, with the owner doing as little as possible (approve in Cursor chat
when present; Slack is optional digest / backup).

## Where your tasks live

Every scheduled or on-demand run: read **your department rule** in `.cursor/rules/<dept>-agent.mdc`
and execute the **Scheduled run** section (or **Morning/Evening run** for Data). Shared P0
outbound scan: `docs/agents/checklists/p0-outbound-scan.md`. Automations in Cursor only trigger
timing; they do not replace these files.

## Non-negotiable guardrails (every task)

- **Never push to `main` directly.** Work on a branch, open a PR. Follow `ship-via-pr` skill.
- **Label every PR `agent`** so native auto-merge can enable. Add your department label too
  (e.g. `content`, `cro`, `data`, `tech`, `design`, `qa`, `analytics`).
- **Auto-merge only when ALL required checks are green**: CI (typecheck, lint, format, build),
  Lighthouse budgets, broken-link check. Never bypass, never merge red.
- **Verify the Vercel preview** looks correct before promoting; production auto-rolls back on
  health degradation (`.github/workflows/post-deploy-health.yml`).
- **Small, focused PRs.** One concern per PR. Keep TypeScript strict; no `any`.
- **Respect layer boundaries** (`src/features` & `src/lib` must not import `@/app/*`).

## The one human carve-out — price/fact verification gate

Any researched price, spec, or factual claim (saldering, subsidies, regulation) MUST go
through the `price-fact-verification` skill. Small in-margin price moves may auto-update;
large deviations or new claims need **explicit owner approval with source citation**.

### Where approval happens (priority order)

1. **Cursor chat (preferred when owner is in the conversation):** If the owner clearly
   approves in this chat (e.g. "✅", "doe maar", "akkoord", "goedkeuren"), **execute
   immediately**. Do not wait for a Slack ✅. Do not ask them to repeat the approval in Slack.
2. **Slack 🔒:** Only when the owner is **not** in an active Cursor chat that can approve
   (scheduled Cloud Agent runs, overnight jobs). Then use the 🔒 template + PR URL + EXECUTE.
3. Never auto-publish unverified facts without one of the above.

## KPIs you optimize for

- **Primary:** outbound clicks to merchant offers (`offer_clicked`, "Bekijk aanbieders").
- **Secondary:** beslishulp completions, compare usage, product detail views, organic search,
  time on guides. Events live in `src/lib/observability/analytics.ts` (Plausible).

## Reporting

- **In Cursor chat:** Prefer reporting progress and asking for gate approval here when the
  owner started or is active in the conversation. Execute on their ✅ in-chat.
- **Slack:** Optional short digest after a run (what changed, PR link, checks). Use 🔒 Slack
  **only** when Cursor chat cannot get the approval (unattended automation).

### 🔒-goedkeuringen via Slack (alleen unattended)

Owner reageert met ✅ → automation **Slack ✅ execute approval** voert uit. Zonder PR-link
kan die automation niets mergen. Daarom:

1. **Eerst** branch + PR openen (label `agent` + department), ook als publicatie nog wacht.
2. **Daarna** Slack-bericht starten met `🔒`, met **PR-URL**, bron/citaat, en concrete
   `EXECUTE:`-regels (merge PR, DB-stappen, admin-actie).
3. Nooit een 🔒 posten zonder PR-URL, behalve pure admin-only gates (lead/refund) waar geen
   code-PR hoort; dan wel een admin-URL + `EXECUTE:`-regel.
4. Als de owner al in Cursor heeft goedgekeurd: **geen** 🔒 posten; wel optioneel een
   korte "uitgevoerd"-digest zonder actie te vragen.

Sjabloon: `docs/agents/slack-ops.md` en skill `price-fact-verification`.

## Definition of done

Branch + PR opened & labelled → all required checks green → preview verified → (auto-)merged →
production healthy → short summary (Cursor and/or Slack digest).
